What is Deep Learning?

Deep Learning mimics how human brain learn, to give output.

 Imagine number of layers of cardboard stacked on top of other, now each layer process specific features of your input, gradually transforming raw data into meaningful information.
 Suppose, a person is approaching you from far away whom you can't recognize yet.

 NOW,
  When they come closer you notice their basic facial features like edges,curves outline of face.
  As they move closer you begin to identify details like eyes,nose.
  Finally, your brain combines these features and matches them with your memory and  you are able to recognize the person.